        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-27T23:38:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If power_button_is_stable \u003d\u003d 1 and debounced_power_pressed \u003d\u003d 0, after power_button_change_deferred runs (step 4 above), shouldn\u0027t that break out of the loop in power_button_wait_for_release?\n\nIf the waiting task is asleep at that time due to task_wait_event(-1), would it be simpler to wake the task on a false alarm?",
      "parentUuid": "2b35120d_ec369089",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "b105b1117211cb7faff9328114015d0d269953ba",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f79fd838_e1cd1a00",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-27T23:58:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is how to wake the task up.\n\nIf the debounced_power_presssed changes, it notifies the HOOK_POWER_BUTTON_CHANGE hook. This hook registered in the power sequence will wake the task up and then break the loop.\n\nBut on this bug, the debounced_power_presssed doesn\u0027t change, so no hook will be notified. We can\u0027t notify HOOK_POWER_BUTTON_CHANGE, because technically, the power button does not change.\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/refs/heads/master/common/power_button.c#145",
      "parentUuid": "9603f911_b02bf9c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "b105b1117211cb7faff9328114015d0d269953ba",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
